      en: "Othello Tower is a medieval bastion in Famagusta, Cyprus, built in the 14th century by the Lusignans and later reinforced by the Venetians. Its name is linked to Shakespeare's play Othello, which is partly set in Famagusta. The tower is a large circular structure with loopholes and a rooftop platform. It was a key defensive point for the harbor. Today, it serves as a museum and viewpoint, offering panoramic views of the old city.",
