      en: "Kyrenia Castle is a well-preserved medieval fortress located in the harbor of Kyrenia, Cyprus. Originally built by the Byzantines in the 7th century, it was expanded by the Lusignans and Venetians. The castle houses the Shipwreck Museum, featuring an ancient Greek merchant ship from the 4th century BC. Its thick walls, Gothic chapel, and impressive battlements reflect its strategic importance. It served as an administrative center and prison. Now a museum, it attracts many visitors.",
