      en: "The Bedesten is a covered market in Nicosia, originally built as a Byzantine church of Saint Nicholas in the 7th century. It was later converted into a Gothic cathedral and then, under Ottoman rule, used as a covered market. The building combines architectural elements from Byzantine, Gothic, and Ottoman periods. It has a large dome supported by four massive pillars. After restoration in the 2000s, the Bedesten is now used for cultural events. It is located in the heart of Nicosia's old town and is a symbol of the island's turbulent history. The blend of styles reflects the different periods of rule.",
