      en: "Panagia tou Moutoulla (Virgin Mary of Moutoullas) is a Byzantine church in the Troodos Mountains, near the village of Moutoullas. It was built in 1280 and is known for its frescoes, which are among the oldest in the region. The frescoes depict the Virgin and Child, scenes from the life of Jesus, and saints. The church is small, with a steep roof and an apse. It is part of the UNESCO World Heritage Troodos churches. The frescoes show influences from Italian painting. The church is an important testimony to the Byzantine heritage in Cyprus. It is set in a wooded area and is a popular destination for hikers and culture enthusiasts.",
